WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.560
Not for Profit Organisation First Draft tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.960
us to watch out for 7 different&nbsp;
types of misinformation online:

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.880
Satire and parody are funny ways&nbsp;
that we talk about what’s going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.880
in the world. Satire and parody use irony, humour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.600
and sarcasm. This means they can sometimes&nbsp;
fool people into thinking they are real.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.040
False connections happen when headlines&nbsp;
don’t tell the truth about what’s in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.280
article or when the caption&nbsp;
on an image is misleading.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.880
Misleading content uses information that is true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.320
but in a way that makes you draw false&nbsp;
conclusions. It might show opinion as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:41.920
fact or give you a set of facts designed to&nbsp;
have you come to a conclusion that is false.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.920
False context is when real information is shared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:50.360
but the information around it isn’t true.&nbsp;
Real videos with misleading descriptions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:56.760
and images that really depict something&nbsp;
else are easy ways to trick people online.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:03.280
Imposter content is pretending to be something it&nbsp;
isn’t. Videos, images, and even news stories can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:11.160
be faked online. Like the Imposter in Among Us,&nbsp;
not everything online is what it claims to be.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.360
Manipulated content uses altered&nbsp;
images, misleading video edits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:21.600
or other altered content in a way that tricks&nbsp;
you into believing something that isn’t true.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.840
Fabricated content is straight-up faked to&nbsp;
trick you and to manipulate your emotions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:34.200
Even whole videos can be faked using Deep&nbsp;
Fake and Artificial Intelligence technology.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.160
Visit keepitrealonline.govt.nz&nbsp;
for more information.

